From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Antigravity <dev@antigravity.ai>
Date: Sat, 7 Nov 2026 01:00:00 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] rockchip: rk3576: disable u-boot emmc hs200 and hs400 mode

RK3576 eMMC controller (sdhci) in mainline U-Boot has timing tuning
issues in HS200/HS400 mode on various non-Rayson eMMC chips (such as
Longsys/Foresee A3A551 on FriendlyElec NanoPi R76S), causing tuning
execution failed (-5) and boot hangs.

Disable HS200 and HS400 in U-Boot and limit max-frequency to 52MHz so
U-Boot can reliably load the kernel from eMMC. Once booted, the Linux
kernel's own driver and device tree will handle full speed eMMC.

Signed-off-by: Antigravity <dev@antigravity.ai>
---
 arch/arm/dts/rk3576-u-boot.dtsi | 7 +++++++
 1 file changed, 7 insertions(+)

--- a/arch/arm/dts/rk3576-u-boot.dtsi
+++ b/arch/arm/dts/rk3576-u-boot.dtsi
@@ -162,6 +162,13 @@
 	u-boot,spl-sfc-no-dma;
 };
 
+&sdhci {
+	/delete-property/ mmc-hs200-1_8v;
+	/delete-property/ mmc-hs400-1_8v;
+	/delete-property/ mmc-hs400-enhanced-strobe;
+	max-frequency = <52000000>;
+};
+
 &sys_grf {
 	bootph-all;
 };
